```
The `full_name` in `options.data` is read by the `handle_new_user()` Postgres trigger (see `supabase/migrations/0001_profiles.sql`) to seed `profiles.display_name` — do not skip passing it. After signup:
- If `data.session` is present (email confirmation disabled in this Supabase project), redirect straight to `/onboarding/welcome`.
- If `data.session` is `null` (confirmation required), redirect to a "check your email" state (reuse/adapt the existing `/verify-email` UI) instead of assuming the user is logged in.

### 2.6 `apps/web/app/forgot-password/page.tsx` and `apps/web/app/reset-password/page.tsx`
- Forgot password: `supabase.auth.resetPasswordForEmail(email, { redirectTo: `${origin}/reset-password` })`.
- Reset password: read the recovery session Supabase establishes via the URL fragment/callback, then `supabase.auth.updateUser({ password: newPassword })`. Keep existing token-aware `<Suspense>` wrapping from Phase 3 (do not remove it — Prompt 03 added it specifically to fix a build error).

### 2.7 `apps/web/app/auth/callback/route.ts`
Confirm/implement the standard code-exchange handler: read `code` from the query string, call `supabase.auth.exchangeCodeForSession(code)`, then redirect to `/app` (new OAuth/email-confirmation logins) or `/onboarding/welcome` if `profiles` for this user has no bots yet (first-time signal) — reuse whatever onboarding-completion check already exists in `useSession.onboardingComplete`, but source the "is this a first login" signal from the database (e.g., zero rows in `bots` for this `user_id`) rather than trusting a client-only flag, since a fresh signup on a new device would otherwise re-trigger onboarding incorrectly if you rely on `localStorage` alone.

