## 3. Task 2 — Extend `apps/web/lib/bots.ts` with the missing operations

The file already has `listBots`, `getBot`, `createBot`, `updateBotGraph`, `updateBotMeta`, `deleteBot`, `saveBotVersion`. Add:

### 3.1 `duplicateBotRemote(id: string): Promise<Bot>`
Fetch the source bot with `getBot(id)`, deep-clone its graph with the existing `cloneGraph()` util from `apps/web/lib/graph-utils.ts` (already used for exactly this purpose in the mock `duplicateBot` in `workspace-store.ts` — mirror that logic), then call the existing `createBot()` with `{ name: `${source.name} copy`, description: source.description, graph: clonedGraph, tags: source.tags }`. Return the new `Bot`.

### 3.2 `restoreBotVersion(botId: string, versionId: string): Promise<void>`
Fetch the bot (for its `versions`, already returned by `getBot`), find the matching `BotVersion`, deep-clone its `graph` via `cloneGraph()` (never restore a version's graph object by reference — see the exact bug class Prompt 08 fixed for cloning), and call `updateBotGraph(botId, clonedGraph)`. Also call `saveBotVersion(botId, 'Restored', `Restored from ${version.label}`)` afterward so the restore itself becomes a new version snapshot — never silently overwrite history.

### 3.3 `archiveBot` — decide and implement one of two approaches, and document your choice in a code comment:
- **Option A (preferred, minimal schema change):** add an `archived` boolean column via a new migration `supabase/migrations/0005_bot_archive.sql` (`alter table public.bots add column archived boolean not null default false;`), and add `archiveBot(id)` / `unarchiveBot(id)` thin wrappers around `updateBotMeta`-style updates.
